---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../data/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Advanced Usage - NokVault"
  description="Compression, automation, rotation, deletion, and batch workflows with NokVault."
  canonical={`${base}docs/usage/advanced`}
  keywords={['nokvault advanced', 'file watching', 'scheduled encryption', 'key rotation', 'secure delete']}
>
  <h1>Advanced Usage</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Explore compression, auto-encryption, scheduling, key rotation, secure deletion, and batch workflows in {SITE.name}.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="compression">
    <h2 id="compression">Compression</h2>
    <p>Compress files before encryption to save space, especially for text files and archives:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Encrypt with compression
nokvault encrypt large-file.txt --compress

# Compression is automatically detected during decryption
nokvault decrypt large-file.txt.nokvault`}
      lang="bash"
    />
    <p>
      Compression is particularly effective for text files, JSON, XML, and other compressible formats. Binary files may not compress much.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="auto-encryption-with-file-watching">
    <h2 id="auto-encryption-with-file-watching">Auto-Encryption with File Watching</h2>
    <p>Automatically encrypt files when they are created or modified in a directory:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Watch directory and auto-encrypt
nokvault watch ./sensitive --auto-encrypt \\
  --keyfile ~/.keys/master.key \\
  --delay 5s \\
  --exclude "*.tmp"`}
      lang="bash"
    />
    <p>
      The <code>--delay</code> option prevents encrypting files that are still being written. The watcher runs until you stop it with Ctrl+C.
      A symlink watch root is refused at startup; symlink events are rejected and never encrypted. Policy errors print without
      <code>--verbose</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="scheduled-encryption">
    <h2 id="scheduled-encryption">Scheduled Encryption</h2>
    <p>Set up periodic encryption for automated backups and regular encryption tasks:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Encrypt backups every hour
nokvault schedule encrypt ./backups --interval 1h --keyfile ~/.keys/backup.key

# Encrypt daily at midnight (using cron on Linux/macOS)
# Add to crontab: 0 0 * * * nokvault encrypt /path/to/docs --keyfile ~/.keys/master.key`}
      lang="bash"
    />
    <p>
      Scheduled encryption is useful for maintaining encrypted backups of important directories. Each run re-validates the configured path and
      generated outputs before writing; a symlink or escaping output aborts that tick.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="key-rotation">
    <h2 id="key-rotation">Key Rotation</h2>
    <p>
      Re-key an encrypted file by decrypting with the old credential and re-encrypting with a new one (new salt and ciphertext):
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Rotate key for a file
nokvault rotate-key file.nokvault

# Rotate with specific keyfiles
nokvault rotate-key file.nokvault \\
  --old-keyfile ~/.keys/old.key \\
  --new-keyfile ~/.keys/new.key`}
      lang="bash"
    />
    <p>Key rotation is recommended periodically, especially if a key might have been compromised.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="secure-deletion">
    <h2 id="secure-deletion">Secure Deletion</h2>
    <p>Best-effort overwrite and delete sensitive files:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Secure delete with default passes (interactive: type yes)
nokvault secure-delete sensitive-file.txt

# Non-interactive / CI
nokvault secure-delete sensitive-file.txt --yes

# Preview first
nokvault secure-delete sensitive-file.txt --dry-run

# Secure delete with more passes
nokvault secure-delete sensitive-file.txt --yes --passes 7`}
      lang="bash"
    />
    <p>
      This is best-effort on traditional spinning disks. SSD wear leveling, snapshots, and copy-on-write filesystems may retain prior data; it
      is not a guaranteed forensic wipe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="batch-operations">
    <h2 id="batch-operations">Batch Operations</h2>
    <p>Encrypt or decrypt multiple files using shell loops:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Encrypt all .txt files in current directory
for file in *.txt; do
  nokvault encrypt "$file" --keyfile ~/.keys/master.key --no-prompt
done

# Decrypt all .nokvault files
for file in *.nokvault; do
  nokvault decrypt "$file" --keyfile ~/.keys/master.key --no-prompt
done`}
      lang="bash"
    />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="verbose-output">
    <h2 id="verbose-output">Verbose Output</h2>
    <p>Get detailed information about operations:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`# Verbose encryption
nokvault encrypt ./documents --verbose

# Shows progress, file counts, and detailed status`}
      lang="bash"
    />
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
